# ⚠⚠ LOCAL PROMPT SCRATCH — IGNORED IN FULL, AND DELIBERATELY SO.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC (`gh repo view --json isPrivate` -> false). Prompts
# and review commissions are working correspondence: they quote measurements,
# internal reasoning, environment detail and whatever the author happened to
# paste in. Keeping them tracked would create a publication surface that has to
# be vetted file by file, forever, and the owner ruled on 2026-08-15 that the
# complexity is not worth it. NOTHING under prompts/ is version-controlled.
#
# ⚠ An earlier attempt (`816bbb0`) carved out `!prompts/codex/*-round[0-9]*.md`
# so that review commissions would travel with their branch. It was reverted the
# same day, and the three ways it went wrong are worth keeping:
#   1. It un-ignored 30 historical commissions from already-merged PRs, and
#      `prettier --check .` — which honours .gitignore from Prettier 3 — then
#      failed on 28 unformatted files. The gate went REAL_EXIT=1 (2/4 steps) and
#      the `ci` check went red on the PR head. Measured, not predicted.
#   2. It still MISSED round-1 commissions not named `-round<N>` (five files,
#      e.g. `f5-implementation-review.md`) — the exact silent-untracking trap it
#      was written to close.
#   3. Un-ignoring a path does not vet it; it only publishes it.
#
# ⚠ Do not re-add a negation here. If a commission must travel with a branch,
# quote the relevant part into the PR body, which is reviewed before it is
# published. Tool scripts under tools/ ARE version-controlled — ignoring tools/
# once silently dropped new scripts like check-e2e-guardrails.sh — but that
# lesson is about tools/, not about prompts/.
prompts/

# MemPalace per-project files (issue #185)
mempalace.yaml
entities.json

# MCP server registration (machine-specific paths; WSL-native command differs
# from the Windows `command: wsl` variant, so this is not committed)
.mcp.json
